    "options": {
      "A": "Any turn about O works, even if the six parts are not equal or equally spaced.",
      "B": "She must use group-theory language about rotation groups before naming an angle or order.",
      "C": "The smallest angle is $360^\\circ/6 = 60^\\circ$, and the order is $6$.",
      "D": "She should test only for a mirror line through O, and treat that line test as the rotational order."
    },
